Here is the solution. I have identified that the best approach—without completely changing your `DailyLogs` (Daily Entry) structure—is to record the "split point" directly in the **Refueling Form**.

This follows your suggestion but implements it in the `FuelManagement` screen to keep the data centralized. By recording the **Time**, **Total Odometer**, and **KM Driven Today (Before Refueling)**, you will have all the data needed to calculate efficiency and split the daily usage.

